window.CHTML=window.CHTML||{};window.CHTML.cb=window.CHTML.cb||{};window.CHTML.cb[29]={"h":"<h1 data-b=\"1\" id=\"b1\">Reduced-Form Credit Models: Hazard Rates, Defaultable Bonds and CDS (MFE Section 10.4)</h1>\n<div class=\"box keybox\"><div class=\"bt\">Source line — read first</div>\n<p data-b=\"2\"> <strong>Source actually read:</strong> McNeil, Frey and Embrechts (2015), Section 10.4, printed pp. 391–405. All Lemma, Proposition, Example and equation numbers below are MFE’s. Proofs are MFE’s, expanded where steps were skipped; the small numerical tables are my own computations. The chapter does <em>not</em> cover Section 10.5 (stochastic hazard rates) or the affine models of Section 10.6.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 data-b=\"3\" id=\"b3\">Structural versus reduced-form: the one-paragraph difference</h2>\n<p data-b=\"4\">Merton explains <em>why</em> a firm defaults (assets fall below debt). A <em>hazard-rate</em> (reduced-form) model does not: it simply specifies the distribution of the default time <math display=\"inline\"><mi>τ</mi></math> through a hazard function and then prices instruments from it (MFE p. 391). It is less economic, but it is easy to calibrate to the CDS and bond prices observed in the market.</p>\n<h2 data-b=\"5\" id=\"b5\">Hazard function and survival: definitions and derivations (pp. 391–392)</h2>\n<p data-b=\"6\">Let <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> be a random time with df <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math> and survival function <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></math>, with <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> for all <math display=\"inline\"><mi>t</mi></math>. The jump process is <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></math>.</p>\n<div class=\"box keybox\"><div class=\"bt\">Definition 10.4</div>\n<p data-b=\"7\"> Cumulative hazard <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Γ</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mo>ln</mo><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>. If <math display=\"inline\"><mi>F</mi></math> has a density <math display=\"inline\"><mi>f</mi></math>, the hazard function is <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mi>/</mi><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>.</p>\n</div>\n<h5 data-b=\"8\" id=\"b8\">Derivation of the survival formula (10.25).</h5>\n<p data-b=\"9\">Since <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mo>ln</mo><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover></mrow></math>, <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Γ</mi><mi>′</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mi>′</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mi>/</mi><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mi>/</mi><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>. Integrating from <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Γ</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>: <span class=\"math display\">$$\\bar F(t)=\\exp\\Big(-\\int_0^t\\gamma(s)\\,ds\\Big).\\tag{10.25}\n\\;\\;\\text{\\small(29.1)}$$</span></p>\n<h5 data-b=\"10\" id=\"b10\">Why “hazard rate”.</h5>\n<p data-b=\"11\">For small <math display=\"inline\"><mi>h</mi></math>, <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac displaystyle=\"true\"><mrow><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mi>h</mi></mrow></math>. So <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></math> is the probability of defaulting in the next instant <em>given survival so far</em>. Compare: the density <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></math> is the unconditional probability.</p>\n<h5 data-b=\"12\" id=\"b12\">Weibull example (p. 392).</h5>\n<p data-b=\"13\"><math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></math> gives <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>α</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>. For <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> (exponential) the hazard is constant at <math display=\"inline\"><mi>λ</mi></math>; for <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> it falls with time; for <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> it rises.</p>\n<figure data-b=\"14\">\n<img alt=\"Figure\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/fig/f29_weibull.svg\"/>\n<figcaption><strong>Figure 29.1.</strong> Weibull hazard function and survival function for <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow></math> and <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>. A constant hazard (<math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>) is the “memoryless” case used in most CDS calibration. My plot.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<h2 data-b=\"15\" id=\"b15\">Information, filtration and conditional survival (pp. 392–394)</h2>\n<p data-b=\"16\">Investors observe only whether default has happened. The information at <math display=\"inline\"><mi>t</mi></math> is <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>u</mi></msub><mo>:</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math> (10.26).</p>\n<div class=\"box thm\">\n<p data-b=\"17\"><strong>Result 29.1 (Lemma 10.5: what <math display=\"inline\"><msub><mi>ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></math>-measurable variables look like).</strong> Every <math display=\"inline\"><msub><mi>ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></math>-measurable random variable has the form <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></math> for a function <math display=\"inline\"><mi>h</mi></math> on <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">]</mo></mrow></math> and a constant <math display=\"inline\"><mi>c</mi></math>.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"proof\">\n<p data-b=\"18\"><em>Proof.</em> <math display=\"inline\"><msub><mi>ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></math> is generated by <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>u</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></math>, <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></math> and <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></math>, hence by <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></math> and <math display=\"inline\"><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub></math>. So <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>∧</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>. Put <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>h</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math> and <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>. ◻</p>\n</div>\n<p data-b=\"19\"><em>In words:</em> once you know the firm has survived to <math display=\"inline\"><mi>t</mi></math>, nothing else is known — all survivors look alike, so any <math display=\"inline\"><msub><mi>ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></math>-measurable quantity is a constant on <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></math>.</p>\n<div class=\"box thm\">\n<p data-b=\"20\"><strong>Result 29.2 (Lemma 10.6).</strong> For integrable <math display=\"inline\"><mi>X</mi></math>: <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>X</mi><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mfrac displaystyle=\"true\"><mrow><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>X</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"proof\">\n<p data-b=\"21\"><em>Proof.</em> The left side is <math display=\"inline\"><msub><mi>ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></math>-measurable and zero on <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></math>, so by Lemma 10.5 it equals <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></math>. Taking expectations of both sides, <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>X</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>, which gives <math display=\"inline\"><mi>c</mi></math>. ◻</p>\n</div>\n<h5 data-b=\"22\" id=\"b22\">Consequence: conditional survival (10.28)–(10.29).</h5>\n<p data-b=\"23\">Take <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></math> with <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></math>; then <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></math> and <math display=\"block\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>exp</mo><mo form=\"prefix\" maxsize=\"1.8\" minsize=\"1.8\" stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" maxsize=\"1.8\" minsize=\"1.8\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>.</mi></mrow></math></p>\n<div class=\"box thm\">\n<p data-b=\"24\"><strong>Result 29.3 (Proposition 10.7: the compensated default process is a martingale).</strong> <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi></mrow></math> is an <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></math>-martingale.</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"proof\">\n<p data-b=\"25\"><em>Proof.</em> For <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></math> we need <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>E</mi><mo form=\"prefix\" maxsize=\"1.2\" minsize=\"1.2\" stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo form=\"postfix\" maxsize=\"1.2\" minsize=\"1.2\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>. Left side: <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mfrac displaystyle=\"true\"><mrow><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>. Right side: the integral <math display=\"inline\"><mi>X</mi></math> vanishes on <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></math>, so by Lemma 10.6, Fubini, and <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mi>′</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>γ</mi><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover></mrow></math>, <math display=\"block\"><mrow><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mi>.</mi></mrow></math> The two sides agree. ◻</p>\n</div>\n<p data-b=\"26\"><em>Reading:</em> default arrives at the <em>intensity</em> <math display=\"inline\"><mi>γ</mi></math> while the firm survives; the martingale is the surprise component. This is why <math display=\"inline\"><mi>γ</mi></math> is also called the default intensity.</p>\n<h2 data-b=\"27\" id=\"b27\">Risk-neutral pricing, hedging and incomplete markets (pp. 394–399)</h2>\n<h5 data-b=\"28\" id=\"b28\">The rule (10.30).</h5>\n<p data-b=\"29\">The time-<math display=\"inline\"><mi>t</mi></math> price of a pay-off <math display=\"inline\"><mi>H</mi></math> at <math display=\"inline\"><mi>T</mi></math> is <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo form=\"prefix\" maxsize=\"1.2\" minsize=\"1.2\" stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mi>H</mi><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>ℱ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo form=\"postfix\" maxsize=\"1.2\" minsize=\"1.2\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></math>. There are two justifications: absence of arbitrage (first fundamental theorem: a price system is arbitrage-free iff an equivalent martingale measure <math display=\"inline\"><mi>Q</mi></math> exists), and hedging (the price equals the cost of a replicating strategy).</p>\n<h5 data-b=\"30\" id=\"b30\">One-period default model (p. 394).</h5>\n<p data-b=\"31\">A bond pays 1 (no default) or recovers <math display=\"inline\"><mn>0.6</mn></math> (default, LGD <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></math>), <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></math>, price <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.941</mn></mrow></math>. Solving <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0.941</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>1.05</mn></mfrac><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">[</mo><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>q</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>⋅</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>⋅</mo><mn>0.6</mn><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">]</mo></mrow></mrow></math> gives <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0299</mn><mo>≈</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></math> (the real-world <math display=\"inline\"><mi>p</mi></math> is only <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></math>): the market price implies a larger default probability than the historical one, reflecting risk aversion.</p>\n<h5 data-b=\"32\" id=\"b32\">Replication (pp. 395–396).</h5>\n<p data-b=\"33\">A <em>default put</em> pays 1 if the bond defaults, 0 otherwise. Hold <math display=\"inline\"><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> bonds and <math display=\"inline\"><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> cash. We need <math display=\"block\"><mrow><mn>0.6</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1.05</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>10.31</mn><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"></mspace><mn>1.0</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1.05</mn><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.222em\"></mspace><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>10.32</mn><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mi>.</mi></mrow></math> Subtracting, <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.4</mn><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>, so <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2.5</mn></mrow></math> and <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2.5</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>1.05</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>21</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2.381</mn></mrow></math>. Cost today <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2.5</mn><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>0.941</mn><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2.381</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0285</mn></mrow></math>, equal to <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>1.05</mn></mfrac><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>0.03</mn><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0286</mn></mrow></math> (up to rounding of <math display=\"inline\"><mi>q</mi></math>). Because two equations in two unknowns can always be solved, every claim is replicable: the market is <em>complete</em>, <math display=\"inline\"><mi>Q</mi></math> is unique.</p>\n<div class=\"box plainbox\"><div class=\"bt\">Example 10.8: random recovery breaks completeness (p. 396)</div>\n<p data-b=\"34\"> Let the loss be either <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>50</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></math> or <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>30</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></math> on default. Three states, price <math display=\"inline\"><mn>0.941</mn></math> still. Risk-neutral probabilities <math display=\"inline\"><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> (default, LGD 0.5), <math display=\"inline\"><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> (default, LGD 0.3), <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></math> satisfy <math display=\"block\"><mrow><mn>0.941</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac displaystyle=\"false\"><mn>1</mn><mn>1.05</mn></mfrac><mo form=\"prefix\" maxsize=\"1.2\" minsize=\"1.2\" stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>0.5</mn><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>0.7</mn><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo form=\"postfix\" maxsize=\"1.2\" minsize=\"1.2\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"></mspace><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>10.33</mn><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mi>.</mi></mrow></math> One equation, three unknowns: <math display=\"inline\"><mi>Q</mi></math> is not unique. Eliminating, <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac displaystyle=\"false\"><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>1.05</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mn>0.941</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>0.5</mn><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math> and <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.024</mn><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math> (10.34). The default put then has an <em>interval</em> of arbitrage-free prices: with <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></math> at its extremes, <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>inf</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac displaystyle=\"false\"><mn>0.0239</mn><mn>1.05</mn></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.0228</mn></mrow></math> and <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo>sup</mo><mo>=</mo><mfrac displaystyle=\"false\"><mn>0.04</mn><mn>1.05</mn></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.0379</mn></mrow></math> (10.35; my arithmetic gives 0.0228 and 0.0379, which MFE round to 0.023 and 0.038). The hedging system (10.36) has three equations and two unknowns, so no replicating strategy exists.</p>\n</div>\n<p data-b=\"35\">This illustrates the <em>second fundamental theorem</em>: a market is complete iff there is exactly one equivalent martingale measure. In a real market, with random recovery, you cannot remove all the risk by hedging, so you need the physical distribution of the remaining risk.</p>\n<h5 data-b=\"36\" id=\"b36\">When to use which approach (p. 398).</h5>\n<p data-b=\"37\">Risk-neutral pricing is a <em>relative</em> pricing method: good where related instruments trade (CDS, liquid bonds); poor where they do not. For Indian bank loans to small firms, with no liquid market, the older approach — real-world <math display=\"inline\"><mi>P</mi></math> and historical data — is the natural one (my application of MFE’s remark on loans to small and medium enterprises). <em>Martingale modelling</em> (specify dynamics directly under <math display=\"inline\"><mi>Q</mi></math>) guarantees no arbitrage but makes historical data nearly useless for estimating parameters.</p>\n<h2 data-b=\"38\" id=\"b38\">Defaultable bond pricing (pp. 399–401)</h2>\n<p data-b=\"39\">Let <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math> be the price of a defaultable zero-coupon bond of face value 1 and <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></math> the default-free price. The loss given default is <math display=\"inline\"><mi>δ</mi></math>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p data-b=\"40\"><strong>RT (recovery of Treasury):</strong> on default at <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></math> the holder gets <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></math> default-free bonds, paid at <math display=\"inline\"><mi>T</mi></math>.</p></li>\n<li><p data-b=\"41\"><strong>RF (recovery of face value):</strong> the holder gets <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></math> cash <em>at the default date</em>. RF is closer to legal practice (same seniority, same fractional recovery) but gives messier formulas and can produce negative spreads at extreme parameters (p. 400).</p></li>\n</ul>\n<h5 data-b=\"42\" id=\"b42\">Survival claim.</h5>\n<p data-b=\"43\">Under deterministic <math display=\"inline\"><mi>r</mi></math> and a deterministic risk-neutral hazard <math display=\"inline\"><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup></math>, define <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup></mrow></math>. Then <math display=\"block\"><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo form=\"prefix\" maxsize=\"1.2\" minsize=\"1.2\" stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>T</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo form=\"postfix\" maxsize=\"1.2\" minsize=\"1.2\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mo>exp</mo><mo form=\"prefix\" maxsize=\"1.8\" minsize=\"1.8\" stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" maxsize=\"1.8\" minsize=\"1.8\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"2.0em\"></mspace><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>10.37</mn><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mi>.</mi></mrow></math> <em>A defaultable zero-coupon bond with zero recovery is a default-free bond with the discount rate raised by the hazard.</em> Hence the credit spread of a no-recovery bond equals the hazard rate. Under RT the recovery term is <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" maxsize=\"1.2\" minsize=\"1.2\" stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mi>R</mi></mrow></msup><mo form=\"postfix\" maxsize=\"1.2\" minsize=\"1.2\" stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></mrow></math>, so <math display=\"block\"><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>T</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup><mi>.</mi></mrow></math></p>\n<div class=\"box thm\">\n<p data-b=\"44\"><strong>Result 29.4 (Lemma 10.9: value of a payment at default).</strong> <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo form=\"prefix\" maxsize=\"1.8\" minsize=\"1.8\" stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo form=\"prefix\" maxsize=\"1.8\" minsize=\"1.8\" stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><msub><mi>ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo form=\"postfix\" maxsize=\"1.8\" minsize=\"1.8\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>exp</mo><mo form=\"prefix\" maxsize=\"1.8\" minsize=\"1.8\" stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" maxsize=\"1.8\" minsize=\"1.8\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mi>.</mi></mrow></math></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"proof\">\n<p data-b=\"45\"><em>Proof.</em> By Lemma 10.6 the left side equals <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mfrac displaystyle=\"true\"><mrow><msup><mi>E</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>T</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>exp</mo><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>. The density of <math display=\"inline\"><mi>τ</mi></math> is <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>exp</mo><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>, so the numerator is <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></math>. Dividing, <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>s</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mi>/</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></math>, and <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mi>r</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mi>R</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></math>. ◻</p>\n</div>\n<p data-b=\"46\"><em>Reading:</em> sum over all possible default dates <math display=\"inline\"><mi>s</mi></math> of (density of default at <math display=\"inline\"><mi>s</mi></math> given survival to <math display=\"inline\"><mi>t</mi></math>) times (discount factor to <math display=\"inline\"><mi>s</mi></math>).</p>\n<h2 data-b=\"47\" id=\"b47\">CDS pricing and calibration (pp. 401–403)</h2>\n<p data-b=\"48\">A credit default swap has a <em>premium leg</em> (buyer pays <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math> at dates <math display=\"inline\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></math> while the name survives) and a <em>default leg</em> (seller pays <math display=\"inline\"><mi>δ</mi></math> at default if before <math display=\"inline\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></math>). Accrued premium is ignored (p. 402). <math display=\"block\"><mtable><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\" style=\"text-align: right\"><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">prem</mtext></msubsup><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\" style=\"text-align: left\"><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>:</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"2.0em\"></mspace><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>10.39</mn><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd columnalign=\"right\" style=\"text-align: right\"><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">def</mtext></msubsup></mtd><mtd columnalign=\"left\" style=\"text-align: left\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>δ</mi><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></msubsup><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>exp</mo><mo form=\"prefix\" maxsize=\"1.8\" minsize=\"1.8\" stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>s</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo form=\"postfix\" maxsize=\"1.8\" minsize=\"1.8\" stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mspace width=\"2.0em\"></mspace><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>10.40</mn><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></math> Setting them equal defines the fair spread <math display=\"inline\"><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>*</mo></msubsup></math> (10.41). The (10.40) follows from Lemma 29.4; the premium leg uses (10.29).</p>\n<h5 data-b=\"49\" id=\"b49\">Calibration with a flat hazard.</h5>\n<p data-b=\"50\">If one CDS spread <math display=\"inline\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msup></math> is observed and <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo>≡</mo><msup><mover><mi>γ</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msup></mrow></math> is constant, <math display=\"inline\"><msup><mover><mi>γ</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msup></math> solves (10.42). <math display=\"inline\"><msup><mi>V</mi><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">prem</mtext></msup></math> falls and <math display=\"inline\"><msup><mi>V</mi><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">def</mtext></msup></math> rises in <math display=\"inline\"><msup><mover><mi>γ</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msup></math>, <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">def</mtext></msup><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> and <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">prem</mtext></msup><mo>→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> as <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mover><mi>γ</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo>→</mo><mi>∞</mi></mrow></math>, so there is exactly one solution (p. 403). With several maturities one uses piecewise-constant hazards.</p>\n<h5 data-b=\"51\" id=\"b51\">The rule of thumb (10.43)–(10.44).</h5>\n<p data-b=\"52\">For a flat spread curve, constant <math display=\"inline\"><mi>r</mi></math> and equally spaced dates, with short periods, <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mover><mi>γ</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo>≈</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mi>/</mi><mi>δ</mi></mrow></math> and the risk-neutral one-year default probability is <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mover><mi>γ</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msup></mrow></msup><mo>≈</mo><msup><mover><mi>γ</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo>≈</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mi>/</mi><mi>δ</mi></mrow></math>.</p>\n<table data-b=\"53\">\n<caption><strong>Table 29.1.</strong> Flat-hazard calibration with <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow></math> (LGD 60%, i.e. recovery 40%), <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></math>, five years, quarterly premiums. The rule of thumb is accurate to within about 1%. My own computation; the setup follows (10.42).</caption>\n<thead>\n<tr class=\"header\">\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">CDS spread <math display=\"inline\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msup></math></th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\"><math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mi>/</mi><mi>δ</mi></mrow></math> (rule)</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">exact <math display=\"inline\"><msup><mover><mi>γ</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msup></math></th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">1-yr <math display=\"inline\"><mi>Q</mi></math>-PD</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">5-yr <math display=\"inline\"><mi>Q</mi></math>-PD</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr class=\"odd\">\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">50 bp</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">83.3 bp</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">82.9 bp</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">0.83%</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">4.06%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"even\">\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">120 bp</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">200 bp</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">198.8 bp</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">1.97%</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">9.46%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"odd\">\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">300 bp</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">500 bp</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">495.0 bp</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">4.83%</td>\n<td style=\"text-align: left;\">21.9%</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<figure data-b=\"54\">\n<img alt=\"Figure\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/fig/f29_cds.svg\"/>\n<figcaption><strong>Figure 29.2.</strong> The implied hazard rate against the CDS spread: the exact calibration lies almost on <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>δ</mi></mrow></math>. My calculation.</figcaption>\n</figure>\n<h2 data-b=\"55\" id=\"b55\">P versus Q: Berndt et al. (pp. 404–405)</h2>\n<p data-b=\"56\">Berndt et al. (2008) regressed 5-year CDS spreads on 5-year EDFs for 33 912 firm-day observations (US firms, Dec. 2000–Dec. 2004): <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">EDF</mtext></mrow></math> with <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>33</mn></mrow></math> bp, <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.6</mn></mrow></math>, <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.73</mn></mrow></math> (10.45). Neglecting the intercept, <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mi>/</mi><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">EDF</mtext><mo>≈</mo><mn>1.6</mn></mrow></math>, and with <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≈</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mi>/</mi><mi>δ</mi></mrow></math> and <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>≈</mo><mtext mathvariant=\"normal\">EDF</mtext></mrow></math>, <math display=\"block\"><mrow><mfrac><mi>q</mi><mi>p</mi></mfrac><mo>≈</mo><mfrac><mn>1.6</mn><mi>δ</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1.6</mn><mn>0.75</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2.13</mn><mi>.</mi></mrow></math> MFE’s cautions: the 33 bp intercept is implausible; the ratio varies by sector and over time (Figure 10.6); it is higher for high-quality firms (concave relationship).</p>\n<div class=\"box verdictbox\"><div class=\"bt\">Do you need the original?</div>\n<p data-b=\"57\"> <strong>For the set-up, proofs, bond/CDS pricing and the P–Q ratio: no.</strong> I have followed MFE pp. 391–405 closely. <strong>Open MFE</strong> (printed p. 396, Example 10.8) if you will lecture on market incompleteness. <strong>Read Berndt et al. (2008)</strong> if you cite their regressions in a thesis chapter; only MFE’s summary is in the folder.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 data-b=\"58\" id=\"b58\">What it means for the thesis (my inference)</h2>\n<p data-b=\"59\">Banks’ borrowers are mostly unlisted and have no CDS, so a calibration like Table 29.1 cannot be run directly. But the hazard framework gives you the right vocabulary: a climate shock can be modelled as a rise in <math display=\"inline\"><mi>γ</mi></math> for exposed sectors, with <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Γ</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math> the cumulative effect. The wedge <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math> also warns that a market-implied default probability overstates the loss a bank should provision for.</p>\n<h2 class=\"unnumbered\" data-b=\"60\" id=\"b60\">Check yourself</h2>\n<div class=\"qlist\">\n<p data-b=\"61\">Define <math display=\"inline\"><mi>Γ</mi></math>, <math display=\"inline\"><mi>γ</mi></math> and write <math display=\"inline\"><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover></math> in terms of <math display=\"inline\"><mi>γ</mi></math>.</p>\n<p data-b=\"62\">State Lemma 10.6 and Proposition 10.7.</p>\n<p data-b=\"63\">What is the rule of thumb linking CDS spread and default probability?</p>\n<p data-b=\"64\">Why does <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></math> differ from <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></math>?</p>\n<p data-b=\"65\">Why is the one-period default model complete and Example 10.8 not?</p>\n<p data-b=\"66\">Why is RF closer to legal practice but harder to price than RT?</p>\n<p data-b=\"67\"><math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow></math> constant. Find the 5-year survival probability and the conditional 3-year survival of a bond that has survived 2 years.</p>\n<p data-b=\"68\">A CDS pays 150 bp, LGD is 60%. Estimate the 1-year risk-neutral PD.</p>\n<p data-b=\"69\">Use <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1.6</mn><mi>/</mi><mi>δ</mi></mrow></math> with <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow></math>. If a bank’s historical PD estimate for a firm is 2%, what market-implied PD would you expect, and why should you be careful using it for provisioning?</p>\n<p data-b=\"70\">Prove that the exponential distribution is memoryless using the hazard function.</p>\n<p data-b=\"71\">A colleague says: “CDS spreads are default probabilities.” Correct this using the chapter.</p>\n</div>\n<h3 class=\"unnumbered\" data-b=\"72\" id=\"b72\">Answer sketches</h3>\n<div class=\"alist\">\n<p data-b=\"73\"><math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mo>ln</mo><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover></mrow></math>, <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mi>/</mi><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mi>Γ</mi><mi>′</mi></mrow></math>, <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>exp</mo><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>.</p>\n<p data-b=\"74\">Lemma 10.6: <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>X</mi><mo>∣</mo><msub><mi>ℋ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>X</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mi>/</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>. Prop. 10.7: <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>t</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"false\">}</mo></mrow></msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>u</mi></mrow></math> is a martingale.</p>\n<p data-b=\"75\"><math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mover><mi>γ</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msup><mo>≈</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mi>/</mi><mi>δ</mi></mrow></math> and <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mi>/</mi><mi>δ</mi></mrow></math>.</p>\n<p data-b=\"76\"><math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>; <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow></mrow></math>. They are related by <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>γ</mi><mover><mi>F</mi><mo accent=\"true\">‾</mo></mover></mrow></math>.</p>\n<p data-b=\"77\">Two states and two unknowns give a unique replicating portfolio; three states and two unknowns do not, and <math display=\"inline\"><mi>Q</mi></math> is a set of measures.</p>\n<p data-b=\"78\">RF pays at the default date, so its value depends on the timing of default (Lemma 10.9 integral); RT pays at <math display=\"inline\"><mi>T</mi></math> and is a combination of <math display=\"inline\"><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> and the survival claim.</p>\n<p data-b=\"79\"><math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9048</mn></mrow></math>; conditional 3-year survival <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.06</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9418</mn></mrow></math> (independent of age, because the hazard is constant).</p>\n<p data-b=\"80\"><math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>0.015</mn><mi>/</mi><mn>0.6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2.5</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></math>.</p>\n<p data-b=\"81\"><math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>q</mi><mi>/</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.67</mn></mrow></math>, so <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>5.3</mn><mi>%</mi></mrow></math>. Because <math display=\"inline\"><mi>q</mi></math> includes a risk premium, it exceeds the physical PD and would over-provision.</p>\n<p data-b=\"82\"><math display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>∣</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo>exp</mo><mrow><mo form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mo form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>λ</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></math>, independent of <math display=\"inline\"><mi>t</mi></math>.</p>\n<p data-b=\"83\">A spread compensates for expected loss <em>and</em> risk, so <math display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>*</mo></msup><mi>/</mi><mi>δ</mi></mrow></math> is a risk-neutral, not a physical, default probability, and only a rough proxy (MFE p. 403).</p>\n</div>\n","s":[[201,"b3"],[201,"b5"],[202,"b15"],[203,"b27"],[204,"b38"],[205,"b47"],[206,"b55"],[206,"b58"]]};